abstract: >-
  Evolution by Emergence is an open research corpus and machine-auditable
  candidate architecture for resource-constrained cumulative evolution. Version
  v22.0 retains the v21 universal retained-organization/accessibility and
  cumulative-reproduction core and closes the intelligent-system specialization
  with audited Anchor-Safety, reflexive self-model, shared-layer, and
  correction-preserving transition results. The release title uses "simulation
  of reality" to mean the internal model through which a system experiences and
  acts in the world, not a claim that reality itself is simulated. Formal
  verification establishes implications under explicit premises; empirical,
  causal, political and normative interpretations remain open.
keywords:
  - cumulative evolution
  - emergence
  - retained organization
  - accessibility
  - complex systems
  - Lean
  - corrigibility
  - Anchor-Safety
  - self-model
  - shared intelligence
  - SCAP
